# Q28 regression pin — an enum VARIANT carrying `Float32` payloads must
# round-trip through construction and `match` with no precision loss, and
# arithmetic on the extracted f32 (`x + 0.5f32`) must be exact.
#
# This is the exact shape `canvas/src/event.rx` was forced AWAY from (its
# `PointerMove(Int, Int)` carries a TODO: "return to Float32 payloads once
# enum float payloads work"). Sub-pixel values (120.5, 84.25) would be
# truncated if the payload were Int, and read as garbage if the f32 were
# stored as 8 bytes but loaded as 4. Both backends share the MIR
# `SetField`/`GetField` typed slot path, so this is backend-agnostic.
#
# The load-from-local / bare-f64-literal shapes (which DID miscompile to 0
# before the Q28 fix) are pinned with their own RUN+stdout assertions in
# 650_f32_field_store_via_local and 651_enum_f32_payload_via_local.
#
# NOTE: deliberately ONE payload-carrying construction. Three or more by-value
# constructions of a Float-payload enum variant in one function trip an
# UNRELATED drop-elaboration crash (Q31; reproduces with inline f32 payloads
# and zero coercion), so an e2e pin must not depend on that.
enum Event
  PointerMove(Float32, Float32)
  CloseRequested
end

def handle(e: Event) -> nil
  match e
    Event.PointerMove(x, y) ->
      let sx = x + 0.5f32
      puts "move #{x},#{y} sx=#{sx}"
    Event.CloseRequested -> puts "close"
  end
end

def main
  handle(Event.PointerMove(120.5f32, 84.25f32))
end
